# ============================================================
# Text files — normalise line endings to LF in the repo
# ============================================================
*.py        text eol=lf
*.sh        text eol=lf
*.md        text eol=lf
*.txt       text eol=lf
*.yml       text eol=lf
*.yaml      text eol=lf
*.json      text eol=lf
*.csv       text eol=lf
*.awk       text eol=lf
*.ros       text eol=lf
Makefile    text eol=lf
# SVG is XML — store as text
*.svg       text eol=lf
# ============================================================
# Binary blobs — plain binary, NOT Git LFS
# ============================================================
# LFS was declared here and never used. No LFS server was ever configured, and
# Sherlock has no git-lfs at all, so every export it committed went in as raw
# bytes. Locally the filter then rewrote those same bytes into a 131-byte
# pointer that referenced an object no server holds, which made the working
# tree permanently dirty and blocked every rebase. Staging one would have
# destroyed a 229,602-byte export.
#
# So these are marked binary and nothing more. Large files stay out of git by
# .gitignore, which is the mechanism this project actually relies on.
# Model weights
*.h5        binary
*.hdf5      binary
# NumPy / dataset arrays
*.npz       binary
*.npy       binary
# Archives
*.tar.*     binary
*.zip       binary
*.gz        binary
# Raster images
*.png       binary
*.jpg       binary
*.jpeg      binary
*.gif       binary
# Documents
*.pdf       binary